00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:46.880
2026, under the published rules. Now, here's something that most retail investors get wrong,

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:53.120
and it cost me money before I figured it out. Imagine you already own a rental condo in Toronto,

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:58.400
and last month's rent increased notice pushed your cash on cash yield below 4%.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:04.160
The actual mechanics between that notice and your net return involve mortgage interest deductibility,

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:09.960
capital gains inclusion rates, and REIT distribution tax treatment that most DIY investors

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:16.240
miscalculate. Publicly traded REITs, such as Rio Can or Canadian apartment REIT, deliver monthly

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:22.820
distributions taxed as ordinary income inside a non-registered account, yet flow through tax deferred

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:30.280
in an RRSP. A direct rental property forces you to track adjusted cost-base and claim CCA only on the

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:36.260
building portion. Mortgage investment corporations add another layer because they pool first and second

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:43.400
mortgage debt, and pay out interest income that is fully taxable. The BRRRR strategy adapted for

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:50.300
Canada requires a 20% down payment on the refinance leg, and must clear the stress test rate at the time

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:56.580
of renewal. Professionals always compare after tax internal rates of return across the three vehicles

00:07:56.580 --> 00:08:03.080
before allocating fresh TFSA room. The common misconception is that direct rental property always

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:09.380
beats REITs because of control. The one sentence fix is to run the after-tax cash flow and total

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:15.360
return numbers for each option on the same spreadsheet before committing capital. Before we wrap,

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:21.180
open your brokerage screener, filter for tech names with revenue per employee above $2 million,

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:28.600
then check each against its 50-day moving average and 20-day volume. Flag any that also sit above

